Gross profit is not a line item that banks report, and Bank of America's income statement has no cost of goods sold from which to derive it. The bank reports net interest income, noninterest income, provision for credit losses, and noninterest expense instead, so the measure does not exist for this company.

The closest equivalent is total revenue, net of interest expense, which was about $101.9 billion in fiscal 2024. That is a different measure from gross profit, so I am not using it as the answer.

